  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🧴 Skincare Brand Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Names for a skincare line, body care brand or small-batch apothecary."
    },
    "intro": "Good skincare brand names are short, look clean on a small label, and hint at what the product feels like or is made from: Balm & Bloom, The Beeswax Apothecary, Studio Retinol. The **Skincare Brand Name Generator** suggests names for a skincare (or skin care) brand, body care line or small-batch business: catchy, cute, modern, luxury, aesthetic, natural and botanical, your town or your own name.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Eight good skincare brand names",
        "content": "<p>All eight came from the generator:</p><ul><li><strong>Balm & Bloom</strong>: soft alliteration that suits a gentle range.</li><li><strong>Clean Slate Skin</strong>: a catchy promise in three short words.</li><li><strong>Studio Retinol</strong>: modern and science-led, named after an active ingredient.</li><li><strong>Pearl Botanicals</strong>: a luxury name with plants in it.</li><li><strong>No. 9 Apothecary</strong>: a numbered name that looks good on a small bottle.</li><li><strong>Dewdrop Skin</strong>: cute and easy to remember.</li><li><strong>Oat & Elderflower Naturals</strong>: two real ingredients, so customers know what's inside.</li><li><strong>Sage Skin Goods</strong>: an aesthetic name with a calm colour in it.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "How skincare names work",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Ingredient names</strong> say what's in the jar: <em>The Beeswax Apothecary</em>, <em>Camellia Skin Kitchen</em>. Only name an ingredient the product really contains.</li><li><strong>Science names</strong> use lab and formula words: <em>Formula Labs</em>, <em>Serum Lab Skin Co.</em></li><li><strong>Luxury</strong> names use a number, a pearl or \"atelier\": <em>No. 11 Skin Atelier</em>.</li><li><strong>Apothecary</strong> is an old word for a pharmacist's shop, and suits small-batch, plant-based ranges.</li></ul><p>Labels are small, so a one- or two-word name with \"Skin\" or \"Skincare\" in the descriptor line often works better than a long name.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Check it's free before you print the sign",
        "content": "<p>Press <strong>Check</strong> on any name, or paste one into the <a href=\"../business-name-checker.html\">Business Name Checker</a>, to see whether the domain and social handles are free and to jump to the company register and trade mark searches. Then:</p><ul><li><strong>Search the company register.</strong> In the UK that's Companies House; in the US, your state's business register.</li><li><strong>Search trade marks</strong> with the UK Intellectual Property Office or the USPTO, especially if you'll sell products or open more than one site.</li><li><strong>Look locally.</strong> Search Google Maps for skincare brands near you: a similar name a few streets away will confuse customers even if it's legally fine.</li><li><strong>Get the trade mark search right.</strong> Cosmetics are a crowded trade mark class, and a brand is harder to change once it's printed on stock.</li><li><strong>In the UK, cosmetics have their own rules.</strong> Before you sell, each product needs a UK-based Responsible Person and a safety assessment, and must be notified through the government's cosmetic product notification service.</li></ul><p>This is general guidance, not legal advice. For more on choosing and checking a name, read our guide: <a href=\"../guides/business-naming-best-practices.html\">Business Naming Best Practices</a>.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Naming the range as well as the brand",
        "content": "<p>Many small brands give each product a short name of its own (a cleanser called after a place, a balm called after a flower) under one brand name. Keep the brand name simple so the product names have room. For candles or soap to sit alongside it, try the <a href=\"candle-business-name-generator.html\">Candle Business Name Generator</a> and the <a href=\"soap-business-name-generator.html\">Soap Business Name Generator</a>; for colour cosmetics, the <a href=\"makeup-brand-name-generator.html\">Makeup Brand Name Generator</a>.</p><p>For more, see all the <a href=\"../categories/biz_beauty-names.html\">beauty and wellness business name generators</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What are good skincare brand names?",
        "answer": "Short names that look clean on a label and hint at the product: Balm & Bloom, Oat & Elderflower Naturals, Studio Retinol or No. 9 Apothecary. Choose a style for names like these."
      },
